// Cycle 0 (start): Z, q, r are formed and loaded (z = -r, Y = Y0); cycles 1 .. 5: one rotation each;
// Latency 6 = 5 iterations + 1: start in cycle t gives done = 1 (one cycle) and busy = 0 in cycle t + 6.
// y is formed from the working registers (round shift by q + g); it is valid from done and held until the next start is accepted.
// Back to back: a new start may be given in the done cycle (one result every 6 cycles).
